================================================================================
ADDITIONAL TERMS FOR NETWORK RELAY SERVICE
================================================================================

The above MIT License applies to all client software components of this project.
However, the following additional terms apply to the network relay service
infrastructure and its usage:

1. SCOPE OF ADDITIONAL TERMS

   These additional terms apply to:
   - Official relay nodes operated by the Cyber Pet Team
   - The relay node server software and configuration
   - Any network service infrastructure provided by the project

2. PERMITTED USES

   You are permitted to:

   a) Personal and Educational Use
      - Use official relay nodes for personal, non-commercial purposes
      - Use for educational, research, or academic purposes
      - Deploy private relay nodes for personal use (not publicly accessible)

   b) Development and Testing
      - Use official relay nodes during software development
      - Test client applications against official relay nodes
      - Contribute to the project using official infrastructure

   c) Private Deployment
      - Deploy your own relay nodes for private networks
      - Modify relay node software for private use
      - Run relay nodes within your organization (internal use only)

3. RESTRICTED USES

   The following uses require prior written authorization:

   a) Commercial Operation
      - Operating public relay nodes as a commercial service
      - Charging fees for relay node access
      - Incorporating relay nodes into commercial products

   b) Large-Scale Deployment
      - Operating relay nodes serving more than 1,000 concurrent users
      - Providing relay services to third-party applications
      - Running relay infrastructure as a platform service

   c) Competitive Services
      - Using official relay nodes to support competing products
      - Reverse-engineering relay protocols for competing services
      - Building commercial services that depend on official infrastructure

4. USAGE TERMS FOR OFFICIAL RELAY NODES

   When using official relay nodes, you agree to:

   a) Acceptable Use
      - Use relay nodes only for legitimate peer-to-peer communication
      - Comply with all applicable laws and regulations
      - Respect bandwidth and resource limitations

   b) Prohibited Activities
      - Transmitting illegal, harmful, or malicious content
      - Conducting DDoS attacks or network abuse
      - Circumventing access controls or rate limits
      - Using relay nodes for cryptocurrency mining or similar activities
      - Transmitting spam, malware, or unauthorized advertisements

   c) Service Availability
      - Official relay nodes are provided "as-is" without guarantees
      - The project reserves the right to modify or discontinue services
      - Access may be restricted or terminated for policy violations
      - No SLA or uptime guarantees are provided

5. AUTHORIZATION PROCESS

   To obtain authorization for restricted uses:

   - Submit a written request via GitHub Issues
   - Describe your intended use case and scale
   - Provide technical details of your deployment
   - Allow 30 days for review and response

   Authorization may be granted with or without conditions, or denied at
   the project's sole discretion.

6. ENFORCEMENT

   Violation of these additional terms may result in:

   - Immediate termination of relay node access
   - Blocking of IP addresses or peer IDs
   - Legal action for damages or injunctive relief
   - Reporting to relevant authorities for illegal activities

7. MODIFICATIONS

   The Cyber Pet Team reserves the right to modify these additional terms
   at any time. Continued use of official relay nodes after modifications
   constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.

8. CONTACT

   For questions, authorization requests, or to report violations:
   - GitHub Issues: https://github.com/wheesys/cyber-pet/issues

9. SEVERABILITY

   If any provision of these additional terms is found to be unenforceable,
   the remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect.

10. GOVERNING LAW

    These additional terms shall be governed by the laws of the People's
    Republic of China, without regard to conflict of law principles.

